#: ../../../theme-guide.rst:2
msgid "Theme Guide"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../theme-guide.rst:6
msgid "Key principle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../theme-guide.rst:8
msgid ""
"**Highlight.js themes are language agnostic.** Instead of trying to make a "
"*rich* set of highlightable classes look great in a handful of languages we "
"have a *limited* set of classes that work well for many languages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../theme-guide.rst:12
msgid "Hence, there are two important implications:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../theme-guide.rst:14
msgid ""
"Highlight.js themes can tend to be minimalistic (this has improved over "
"time)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../theme-guide.rst:15
msgid ""
"It's not always possible to exactly emulate themes from other highlighting "
"engines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../theme-guide.rst:19
msgid "Defining a theme"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../theme-guide.rst:21
msgid ""
"A theme is a single CSS file defining styles for the scopes listed in the :"
"doc:`scopes reference </css-classes-reference>`. The general guideline is to "
"style the core/common set of classes, however an author may deliberately "
"choose to exclude some (for example, ``.attr`` is usually left unstyled).  "
"Use our :ref:`auto-check<autocheck>` tool to provide additional guidance on "
"this."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../theme-guide.rst:27
msgid ""
"You are not required to invent a separate styling for every group of class "
"names, it's perfectly okay to group them:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../theme-guide.rst:32
msgid ""
".hljs-string,\n"
".hljs-section,\n"
".hljs-selector-class,\n"
".hljs-template-variable,\n"
".hljs-deletion {\n"
"  color: #800;\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../theme-guide.rst:40
msgid "Use as few or as many unique style combinations as you want."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../theme-guide.rst:46
msgid "Auto-checking your theme"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../theme-guide.rst:48
msgid ""
"We provide a tool to auto-checking your theme to see that it provides good "
"scope coverage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../theme-guide.rst:52
msgid "./tools/checkTheme.js src/styles/your_theme.css"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../theme-guide.rst:54
msgid "Follow the simple guidance provided to fix any issues."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../theme-guide.rst:57
msgid "Theming dos and don'ts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../theme-guide.rst:59
msgid "Don't use:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../theme-guide.rst:61
msgid "non-standard borders/margin/paddings for the root container ``.hljs``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../theme-guide.rst:62
msgid "specific font faces"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../theme-guide.rst:63
msgid ""
"font size, line height and anything that affects position and size of "
"characters within the container"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../theme-guide.rst:66
msgid "Okay to use:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../theme-guide.rst:68
msgid "colors (obviously!)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../theme-guide.rst:69
msgid "italic, bold, underlining, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../theme-guide.rst:70
msgid "image backgrounds"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../theme-guide.rst:72
msgid ""
"These may seem arbitrary at first but it's what has shown to make sense in "
"practice."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../theme-guide.rst:75
msgid ""
"There's also a common set of rules that *must* to be defined for the root "
"container verbatim:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../theme-guide.rst:80
msgid ""
".hljs {\n"
"  display: block;\n"
"  overflow-x: auto;\n"
"  padding: 0.5em;\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../theme-guide.rst:86
msgid ""
"If your theme lives within the core project you do not need to add these "
"rules by hand as they are added by default during the build process."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../theme-guide.rst:91
msgid "``.subst``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../theme-guide.rst:93
msgid ""
"One important caveat: don't forget to style ``.subst``. It's used for parsed "
"sections within strings and almost always should be reset to the default "
"color:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../theme-guide.rst:98
msgid ""
".hljs,\n"
".hljs-subst {\n"
"  color: black;\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../theme-guide.rst:105
msgid "Contributing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../theme-guide.rst:107
msgid ""
"You should include a comment at the top of the CSS file with attribution and "
"other meta data if necessary. The format is free:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../theme-guide.rst:112
msgid ""
"/*\n"
"\n"
"Fancy style (c) John Smith <email@domain.com>\n"
"\n"
"*/"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../theme-guide.rst:118
msgid "Also update CHANGES.md with your contribution."
msgstr ""

